  <h2>The Professional Services Copywriting Framework</h2>

  <p>
    Professional services content follows a consistent pattern:
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li><strong>Lead with expertise</strong> — Demonstrate knowledge before asking for the meeting.</li>
    <li><strong>Address the real concerns</strong> — Clients worry about cost, competence, and fit. Address all three.</li>
    <li><strong>Show outcomes, not just services</strong> — What results do clients actually get?</li>
    <li><strong>Make the consultation valuable</strong> — Position the initial call as worth their time regardless of whether they hire you.</li>
  </ol>

